# `_break_hr1` skips the half-row pair max (the cells marked `hr1_fail` fail)
# and `_break_hr3` writes both threads' P at half 0's columns (every cell with
# at most 16 softmax rows fails); `_break_hr5` swaps the logical ballot halves
# (the padded logical cell fails); `_break_hr6` sends every split to split 0's
# keys and `_break_hr7` shortens every split by one page (the forced multi-split
# cells fail); `_break_p6_5` skips the rope column group of the direct gather
# and `_break_p6_8` stores prefetched indices one tile early (the cells naming
# them in `p6_fail` fail). `_pdl_nowait` drops the split-K decode's grid wait (the
# late-producer cells fail); `_pdl_reuse_break` triggers the next decode from
# the combine's entry, which the wait must still order (every cell passes),
# and `_pdl_reuse_break_nowait` drops the wait too (the late-producer cells
# fail; the reuse cells report whether the race was reached);
# `_ragged_exit_break1` drops the combine's deferred ragged exit and
# `_ragged_exit_break2` the non-split decode's (the short-batch cells at
# forced np 3, resp. np 1, fail). `_cg2_slice_break1` and `_cg2_slice_break2`
# hand the default h=128 pair's follower the leader's V depth slice or key
# half (the pair cells, which `MLA_CG2_SLICE_BREAK` alone runs, fail). They
# and every other `_cg2*` arm set `MLA_SPARSE_CG2_ROUTE=0`, so short cells stay
# on the pair rather than routing to the unpaired kernel;
