# 3=swcausal,4=swnoncausal); `-D FA4_1Q_SPLITK_DEPTH` selects head_size.
# Committed (gates the M4 sign-off): {null,causal} x {64,128} x P{2,4,6,8,10}.
# P=6 (cache 3072) and P=10 (cache 5120) are the non-pow2 cluster sizes; the
# combine is P-general (all P partitions write their own, possibly uneven, band).
# Discovery (start_column>0; chunked@P8 also exercises M6 empty partitions):
# {chunked,swcausal,swnoncausal} x {64} x P{2,4,6,8,10}.
# depth=128 (M4.4 / #36): TWO independent depth-128 bugs, both now FIXED, so
# ALL masks pass and are committed (no `manual` targets remain):
#   1. The split-KV load path (num_qk_stages=2, depth>=128) did not window its
#      per-partition tile count, so the producer over-filled the K/V pipeline vs
#      the windowed consumers and deadlocked. Fixed in load_warp.mojo (window the
#      iter count). This unhung {null,causal} x 128.
#   2. `fa4_splitk_combine_write` sized its combined-O register buffer `o_final`
#      for ONE depth-column, but depth 128 has iters_total==2, so the 2nd column
#      clobbered the 1st (see the windowed-mask block below for the full writeup).
#      This is what made the WINDOWED masks (chunked/SW) mismatch at depth 128.
# {null,causal,chunked,swcausal,swnoncausal} x 128 x P all PASS at the bf16 floor
# (0.0039). SM100-only (B200).
